**What stays in `src/services/appointment.service.ts`**

Keep it as the facade only:

```txt
imports
export type { AppointmentActor }
export { assertAppointmentConfirmationModeAllowed }
export const appointmentService = { ... }
export const appointmentInternalService = { ... }
```

After moving, the main file should become something like:

```ts
export type { AppointmentActor } from "./appointment/appointment.types";
export { assertAppointmentConfirmationModeAllowed } from "./appointment/appointment-validation.service";

export const appointmentService = {
  getAutoConfirmSettings: appointmentSettingsService.getAutoConfirmSettings,
  updateAutoConfirmSettings: appointmentSettingsService.updateAutoConfirmSettings,
  updateSettings: appointmentSettingsService.updateSettings,

  checkAvailability: appointmentQueryService.checkAvailability,
  list: appointmentQueryService.list,
  calendar: appointmentQueryService.calendar,
  detail: appointmentQueryService.detail,

  create: appointmentCreateService.create,
  createAppointmentFromValidatedInput,
  rescheduleAppointmentFromValidatedInput,

  reschedule: appointmentRescheduleService.reschedule,
  requestReschedule: appointmentRescheduleService.requestReschedule,
  approveRescheduleRequest: appointmentRescheduleService.approveRescheduleRequest,
  declineRescheduleRequest: appointmentRescheduleService.declineRescheduleRequest,

  confirm: appointmentOutcomeService.confirm,
  cancel: appointmentOutcomeService.cancel,
  complete: appointmentOutcomeService.complete,
  noShow: appointmentOutcomeService.noShow,
  missed: appointmentOutcomeService.missed,

  assign: appointmentAssignmentService.assign,
  claim: appointmentAssignmentService.claim,

  getAppointmentContextForAi: appointmentQueryService.getAppointmentContextForAi,
};
```

Start with phases 1-3 first. Once those compile, then move create/reschedule/outcome/assignment. That order will save you a lot of import chaos.